Looking at your code, I can see the issue. The tab pages are being covered by the sidebar because of a CSS conflict with the .main-content styling. The main issue is that the sidebar has a fixed position and width, but the main content area isn't properly accounting for it.

Here are the specific problems and solutions:

Problem 1: Main content width calculation

The .main-content class has:

```css
.main-content {
    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
    width: calc(100% - var(--sidebar-width));
}
```

This should work, but there might be conflicts with Bootstrap's container-fluid and row classes.

Solution: Update your CSS

Replace your existing .main-content and related styles with these fixes:

```css
/* Main Content - FIXED */
.main-content {
    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
    padding: 30px;
    transition: var(--transition);
    min-height: 100vh;
    width: calc(100% - var(--sidebar-width));
    overflow-x: hidden; /* Changed from auto to hidden */
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
}

/* Ensure container-fluid doesn't cause overflow */
.container-fluid {
    padding: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
}

/* Fix for row within main-content */
.main-content .row {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
    width: 100%;
}

/* Ensure all cards and content stay within bounds */
.main-content .card,
.main-content .col-md-*,
.main-content .col-* {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
}

/* Fix for the specific chart container that might be causing issues */
.main-content .col-md-8,
.main-content .col-md-4 {
    padding-left: 15px;
    padding-right: 15px;
}

/* Mobile responsiveness fix */
@media (max-width: 992px) {
    .main-content {
        margin-left: 70px;
        width: calc(100% - 70px);
        padding: 20px;
    }
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .main-content {
        margin-left: 0;
        margin-bottom: 70px;
        width: 100%;
        padding: 15px;
    }
}
```

